# Without this file the worker image does not build at all.
#
# apps/worker/Dockerfile does `COPY packages ./packages` and `COPY apps/worker ./apps/worker`
# from the repo root, so the whole working tree is sent as build context. pnpm's node_modules is
# a farm of symlinks into .pnpm/, and Docker refuses to load them:
#
#   ERROR: invalid file request apps/worker/node_modules/@anthropic-ai/sdk
#
# Even where it does not error, shipping host node_modules into the image is wrong twice over:
# they are Windows/darwin builds being copied into a linux container, and they would shadow the
# Linux dependency tree the build stage installs from the lockfile.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output — regenerated inside the image.
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
out
**/out
*.tsbuildinfo

# Never send secrets or local state to the daemon.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Nothing here affects the runtime image; excluding it keeps the context small.
.git
.github
.vscode
.idea
coverage
playwright-report
test-results
docs
*.log
README.md
